In article <1993Feb19.091825.27105@abekrd.co.uk> mike@abekrd.co.uk (Mike Quinn) writes:

   I disagree with the poster who suggested that the mines were too hard for
   a starting character - they're perfect. A mini, self-contained dungeon with
   plenty to kill, plenty to collect, shops, an altar and a useful little 'gray'
   gem at the end. If your character can clear the Gnomish mines, you actually
   stand a chance with the rest of the dungeon, all in under 10K moves.

I have found that to be pretty much depending on what class you play.
I usually play barbarian (simply because I enjoy winning - the other
classes are a lot harder to me), and then 3.1 is a LOT easier than
3.0, because you almost always survive the mines with a low level
character, and once out of them you're off to a splendid start, and
way ahead compared to 3.0.

If, on the other hand, I play something weak (say healer, I just can't
figure out how to do well with one), I die instantly on entering the
mines, and, accordingly, don't. But then the Dungeons of Doom are so
much harder, because you simply need a lot of the stuff from the
mines. So in this way I find 3.1 to be less balanced than 3.0. (But,
as stated earlier, I like winning, so 3.1 is just fine :-))



